          ],
          "correct": 2,
          "explanation": "<p>(i) 6x<sup>2</sup> + 14x + 8 = 0</p>\n<p>6x<sup>2</sup> + 8x + 6x +8 = 0</p>\n<p>6x(x + 1) +8(x + 1) = 0</p>\n<p>(6x + 8) (x + 1) = 0</p>\n<p>X = -1, <span class=\"math inline\">\\(- \\frac{8}{6}\\)</span></p>\n<p>(ii) 3y<sup>2</sup> + 7y + 4 = 0</p>\n<p>3y<sup>2</sup> + 3y +4y + 4 = 0</p>\n<p>3y(y + 1) + 4(Y + 1) = 0</p>\n<p>(y + 1) (3y + 1) = 0</p>\n<p>y = -1 or - 1.33</p>\n<p>x = y</p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "6acb7c97243d5be0d55c8a5a",
          "question": "<p>In the following questions two equations numbered I and II are given. You have to solve both the equations and choose the correct option.</p>\n<p>I.<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>102</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br />II. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>224</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>",
