          ],
          "correct": 1,
          "explanation": "<p>From equation I:<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>11</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>102</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>17</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>17</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></math><br />From equation II:<br />&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>30</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>224</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>14</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn></math></p>\n<p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mtable columnalign=\"left\" rowlines=\"solid\" columnlines=\"solid\" frame=\"solid\"><mtr><mtd/><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>17</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>14</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>y</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>y</mi></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>y</mi></mtd><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><mi>y</mi></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></p>\n<p>So, x &gt; y</p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "6acb7c97243d5be0d55c8a5b",
          "question": "<p>two equations (I) and (II) are given. You have to solve both the equations and give answer.</p>\n<div class=\"ng-tns-c2974603897-6\">\n<div class=\"q-text ng-tns-c2974603897-6\">\n<div><strong>I.</strong>&nbsp;9<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo></math> 26x + 16 = 0</div>\n<div>&nbsp;</div>\n<div><strong>II.</strong>&nbsp;3<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;&ndash; 16y + 20 = 0</div>\n</div>\n</div>\n<div class=\"answere ng-tns-c2974603897-6\">\n<div id=\"opt-A-0\" class=\"col-xs-12 ans-text ng-tns-c2974603897-6\"></div>\n</div>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>x&gt;y</p>",
            "<p>y&gt;x</p>",
            "<p>x<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&ge;</mo></math>y</p>",
            "<p>y<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&ge;</mo></math>x</p>",
            "<p>if x = y or relationship between x and y can't be established</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 3,
          "explanation": "<p>I.&nbsp;9<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;&ndash; 26x + 16 = 0</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&rArr; 9<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&ndash; 18x &ndash; 8x + 16 = 0</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&rArr; 9x (x &ndash; 2) &ndash; 8 (x &ndash; 2) = 0</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&rArr; (9x &ndash; 8) (x &ndash; 2) = 0<br />&nbsp;</p>\n<p>x=8/9 , 2</p>\n<div>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p><br />II.&nbsp;3<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;&ndash; 16y + 20 = 0</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&rArr; 3<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&ndash; 6y &ndash; 10y + 20 = 0</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&rArr; 3y (y &ndash; 2) &ndash; 10 (y &ndash; 2) = 0</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>&rArr; (3y &ndash; 10) (y &ndash; 2) = 0<br />&nbsp;</p>\n<p>y=10/3 , 2</p>\n<p><br /><br />Here, x &le; y</p>\n</div>"
        },
        {
          "id": "6acb7c97243d5be0d55c8a5c",
          "question": "<p>In the following question, two equations I and II are given. Solve both the equations carefully and choose the correct option.</p>\n<p>I: <span class=\"math inline\">\\(x^{2} + 2x - 35 = 0\\)</span></p>\n<p>II: <span class=\"math inline\">\\(y^{2} + 10y + 16\\ = 0\\)</span></p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>x &gt; y</p>",
            "<p>x &lt; y</p>",
            "<p>x &ge; y</p>",
            "<p>x &le; y</p>",
            "<p>x = y or relationship between x and y cannot be determined</p>"
          ],
          "correct": 4,
          "explanation": "<p>I: <span class=\"math inline\">\\(x^{2} + 2x - 35 = 0\\)</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"math inline\">x = -7 or 5</span></p>\n<p>II: <span class=\"math inline\">\\(y^{2} + 10y + 16\\ = 0\\)</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"math inline\">x = -8 or -2</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"math inline\">-8 &lt; -7 &lt; -2 &lt; 5</span></p>\n<p><span class=\"math inline\">The relationship between x and y cannot be determined</span></p>"
        },
        {
          "id": "6acb7c97243d5be0d55c8a5d",
          "question": "<p>In the questions, two equations I and II are given. You have to solve both the equations to establish the correct relation between x and y and choose the correct option.</p>\n<p>I.) 4x<sup>2</sup>&nbsp;+ 24x + 35 = 0</p>\n<p>II.) 8y<sup>2</sup>&nbsp;+ 26y + 15 = 0</p>",
          "image_url": null,
          "images": [],
          "type": "mcq",
          "options": [
            "<p>x &gt; y</p>",
            "<p>x &lt; y</p>",
            "<p>x = y or the relationship cannot be established</p>",
            "<p>x &ge; y</p>",
            "<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">x &le; y</span></p>"
          ],
          "correct": 4,
          "explanation": "<p><strong>Solution</strong></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">From I:</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">4<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&nbsp;+ 24x + 35 = 0</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">4<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&nbsp;+ 14x + 10x + 35 = 0</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">2x(2x + 7) + 5(2x + 7) = 0</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">(2x + 5)(2x + 7) = 0</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">x = -5/2, -7/2</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">From II:</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">8<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&nbsp;+ 26y + 15 = 0</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">8<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">&nbsp;+ 20y + 6y + 15 = 0</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">4y(2y + 5) + 3(2y + 5) = 0</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">(4y + 3)(2y + 5) = 0</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">y = -3/4, -5/2</span></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">So, x &le; y</span></p>"
        },
        {
